From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 02:26:42 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] util: fall back to a container file when POSIX shm is denied

A sandboxed Apple application may only create POSIX shared memory under a
name belonging to an entitled application group, and an iOS application has
no such entitlement: shm_open() returns EPERM for every name. Measured in an
iOS app on macOS in Designed for iPad mode, where shm_open() is denied but an
mmap(MAP_SHARED) over a file in the app temporary directory works and carries
4 MiB through unchanged.

Fall back to an unlinked mkstemp file under TMPDIR, which inside an app
container is that container's own tmp directory. Callers only need a shareable
mapping, which this provides, and the file never appears in the namespace.
Platforms that can create POSIX shared memory keep doing so.
---
 src/mesa/util/anon_file.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mesa/util/anon_file.c b/src/mesa/util/anon_file.c
index 4a48ef2db4ef0c6cfa2ca905dc9ec0c35b158c9f..b00cef36563cd049509bc97d29a78a0546800343 100644
--- a/src/mesa/util/anon_file.c
+++ b/src/mesa/util/anon_file.c
@@ -196,6 +196,15 @@ os_create_anonymous_file(off_t size, const char *debug_name)
      if (errno != EEXIST)
        break;
    }
+   if (fd < 0 && (errno == EPERM || errno == EACCES)) {
+     /* A sandboxed Apple application is not allowed to create POSIX shared
+      * memory unless its name belongs to an entitled application group, and
+      * an iOS application has no such entitlement by default. An unlinked
+      * file in the process temporary directory -- inside the app container,
+      * on the same volume -- maps MAP_SHARED just as well, which is all a
+      * caller of this function needs. */
+     return os_create_unlinked_file(size, "mesa-shared");
+   }
 #elif defined(__OpenBSD__)
    char template[] = "/tmp/mesa-XXXXXXXXXX";
    fd = shm_mkstemp(template);
